  "article_headline": "Prince's Clutch Free Throws Lift STVM Past Walsh Jesuit 54–53",
  "article_dek": "DeCarlo Prince seals the one-point win after the Warriors erase a 15-point deficit late.",
  "article_body": "AKRON, Ohio — St. Vincent–St. Mary survived a late Walsh Jesuit comeback to win 54–53 on February 6, 2026. The Fighting Irish appeared to have control after building a double-digit second-half advantage, but the Warriors made the final minutes a test of composure.\n\nSTVM led 25–20 at halftime, then outscored Walsh 17–9 in the third to take a 42–29 advantage into the fourth. The Warriors responded with a surge that erased a 15-point deficit and put them ahead 53–52 late.\n\nWith the game on the line, senior DeCarlo Prince stepped to the line and made two free throws, restoring a 54–53 STVM lead. Walsh could not release a final shot before time expired, and the Irish held on by a point.\n\nSummit County Sports’ gallery records the action and emotions surrounding the finish through Mason Bybee’s courtside photography.",
